<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-US">
  <break time="2500ms" />
  High-stakes projects often fail in the last mile: requirements are scattered,
  evidence is incomplete, and a checklist can only report the mess.
  <break time="500ms" />
  This is Closeout, an autonomous delivery operations agent running live on
  Google Cloud.
  <break time="500ms" />
  The public Cloud Run application sends an authenticated Cloud Task to a
  private worker. The worker uses Google A D K 2 and Gemini 3.5 Flash through
  Vertex A I, while Firestore preserves durable run state.
  <break time="500ms" />
  Closeout validates a bounded workspace before any agent action. Three bounded
  project artifacts enter the intake.
  <break time="500ms" />
  With one command, it maps obligations, verifies evidence, performs only
  allowlisted reversible repairs, and seals the result. Gemini proposes the
  plan, but deterministic policy controls every side effect.
  <break time="500ms" />
  The asynchronous worker completes in the background and reports eighty-eight
  percent evidence coverage.
  <break time="500ms" />
  Six requirements are verified, one internal gap is repaired, and one public
  video requirement remains honestly blocked. Closeout never turns a generated
  script or a local build into external proof.
  <break time="500ms" />
  Every verdict links to its source and confidence. The audit trace records each
  stage, actor, action, and retry-safe state transition.
  <break time="500ms" />
  Finally, Closeout produces a stable zip with the evidence ledger, audit
  events, artifacts, and S H A 256 manifest.
  <break time="500ms" />
  Closeout is autonomous where actions are bounded, and honest where proof is
  external.
</speak>
